  "title": "The Assumption Under the Floor",
  "family": "learning",
  "category": "work/process",
  "premise": "A planner wants to compare two production routes, but one estimate silently assumes existing voice recordings. Pulling up the floorboard reveals the assumption and recalculating both routes makes the comparison usable.",
  "hook": "What is this estimate standing on?",
  "visible_action": "Two timelines rest on foundation blocks; removing a missing-recording assumption lengthens only the affected path.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "An estimate is easier to evaluate when its key assumptions are visible.",
  "gate": "Use invented times and costs; avoid presenting the toy forecast as a real quote.",
